  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergeny response for indigenous people forcibly displaced to Quibdo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 14 February, at least 111 Katio Indigenous people from the Vivicora community in the Indigenous Resguardo Tahami in Choco Department have been forcibly displaced due to threats to their lives from the ELN guerrilla and the risk to be caught in the crossfire of the combat between the Colombian army and the ELN. Due to this situation at least 962 Indigenous people of 8 communities are in confinement (not able to move, facing lack of access to food, services and goods).
The project will provide emergency response in terms of food and non-food items, as well as psychological support.</narrative>
  </description>
